                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Newberry.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-05-09"><hi rendition="#italic">May 9,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 84.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received Mr. Thompson’s No. 76, of
                    21st ultimo, by which the Department learns with extreme gratification that the
                    Porte has taken action touching censorship of religious books which is
                    satisfactory to the representatives of this missionary interest in Turkey.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
